---
description: Async Python, FastMCP, PostgreSQL and pgvector implementation
globs: "**/*.py, **/*.sql"
alwaysApply: false
---
Keep FastMCP decorators thin. Authenticate first; validate typed input; call domain functions.
Use transaction-local identity, a parameterized query and the same pooled connection.
Assert isolation using the non-owner runtime role, including same-tenant project denial.
Use async I/O, bounded retries and deadlines. Keep external embedding calls outside write locks.
Make duplicate replay safe and payload mismatch a conflict. Preserve decision provenance.
When changing retrieval, compare filtered approximate results with exact cosine ground truth.
